# Personal OS — Cursor Rules

## System Context

Single-user life dashboard. Next.js 14 (App Router) on Netlify, Supabase PostgreSQL. No auth. Content written by AI assistant (Rafa) via API routes.

Monorepo: `apps/web/` (Next.js) + `packages/shared/` (Zod types, utils).

## Adding Features

Every feature follows a 7-step pattern. See `docs/adding-a-new-feature.md` for the full walkthrough. The newsletter feature is the canonical reference.

Steps: Supabase table → Zod types in `packages/shared/src/types/` → API route → page → feature components → briefing widget → nav links (header.tsx + mobile-nav.tsx).

## Key Patterns

- **API responses**: Always include `timestamp: new Date().toISOString()` in every response.
- **POST routes**: Accept single item or array: `Array.isArray(body) ? body : [body]`.
- **Client-side fetching**: All feature components use `'use client'` + `useEffect` → `fetch('/api/...')`.
- **Types**: Import from `@personal-os/shared`. Zod schemas in `packages/shared/src/types/`. Export from barrel `index.ts`.
- **UI primitives**: Use `Button`, `Card`, `Badge`, `Input`, `Select`, `Skeleton`, `Alert`, `Toast` from `@/components/ui`. Use `cn()` from `@/lib/utils`.
- **State handling**: Every list needs loading (Skeleton), error, and empty (EmptyState) states.
- **Navigation**: Duplicated in `header.tsx` and `mobile-nav.tsx` — update both.

## Gotchas

- **No auth** — Intentional. Don't add authentication.
- **Single production DB** — No staging. No migration tool. Tables created via SQL in Supabase dashboard.
- **Tailwind v4** — Uses `@tailwindcss/postcss`, not classic plugin. Surface-* color tokens.
- **Supabase client** — Proxy pattern in `lib/supabase.ts`. Import directly, don't await.
- **Components ≤ 150 lines** — Split if larger.
- **Deploy** — Netlify auto-deploys on merge to `main`.

## Code Style

- PascalCase components, camelCase functions/variables, kebab-case files
- Strict TypeScript — avoid `any`
- Don't create new base UI components — use existing `@/components/ui`
- Prefer existing shared utilities over creating new ones

## Workflow

- Feature branch → PR → squash merge to `main`
- Run `npm run type-check && npm run lint` before pushing

## Reference Files

- `packages/shared/src/types/newsletter.ts` — Zod schema pattern
- `apps/web/src/app/api/newsletters/route.ts` — API route pattern
- `apps/web/src/components/features/newsletters/newsletter-list.tsx` — List component pattern
- `apps/web/src/components/features/briefing/newsletter-section.tsx` — Briefing widget pattern
